    "title": "Former building of 90-year-old Pittsfield restaurant for sale - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natalie St. Denis ,\n1 hours ago\nPITTSFIELD, Mass. ( NEWS10 ) -- A Downtown Pittsfield building that once was home to the renowned Highland Restaurant is for sale. The family-owned business closed at the end of August after operating for 90 years.\nDownload our WTEN+ streaming app on Roku, Fire TV and Apple TV! At the beginning of October, the nearly 13,000-square-foot property was listed for sale . The building, located at 100 Fenn Street, adjacent to City Hall, hit the market for $975,000 . It's situated within the City of Pittsfield's Downtown Creative District and Housing Development Incentive Program (HDIP) Overlay.\nIn the heart of downtown, the building has served as a notable landmark to locals since it was built in 1900. It has a distinguished history as a longtime gathering place for the community.\nGet the latest news, weather, sports and entertainment delivered right to your inbox! The historic Highland Restaurant shared its gratitude for years of support in its closure announcement on social media .\n\"The Highland has always been more than a restaurant. It has been our family's home and life's work. We are endlessly grateful to our employees, with some being with us for more than 50 years, for their loyalty, dedication, and friendship,\" reads the post.\n\"Above all, thank you to the people of Berkshire County and beyond,\" the post continues. \"Your support, kindness, and memories have sustained us for nine decades. We hope The Highland will always be remembered not just for the meals we served, but for the moments shared around our tables.\"\nThe property offers potential for restaurant, hospitality, retail, residential or mixed-use redevelopment. For more information on the listing, call Jim Thurston at 413-329-4780 or email jthurston@lamacchiarealty.com .\nRead the latest from NEWS10:\nNEWS10 is the Capital Region's local news leader!\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
    "summary": "The building, located at 100 Fenn Street, adjacent to City Hall, hit the market for $975,000 . It's situated within the City of Pittsfield's Downtown Creative District and Housing Development Incentive Program (HDIP) Overlay. The historic Highland Restaurant shared its gratitude for years of support in its closure announcement on social media . We are endlessly grateful to our employees, with some being with us for more than 50 years, for their loyalty, dedication, and friendship,\" reads the post. The property offers potential for restaurant, hospitality, retail, residential or mixed-use redevelopment.",
